---
// Based on the old WordPress site's Privacy Policy (technicalsource.com/privacy-policy),
// updated for how this site works (the forms and where they send, the chat
// assistant, analytics, what the browser remembers) and corrected (owner,
// Oct 1, 2026): data stays in the U.S.; no selling; shared only with service
// providers, at your request or when the law requires; no logins, partner
// offers or co-branded sites. Keep the SMS and cookie sections as they are.
// Counsel to review before launch.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Banner from '../components/Banner.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Technical Source collects, uses and protects the personal information you share with us.">
  <Banner eyebrow="Legal" compact>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="banner-sub">Last updated October 2026</p>
  </Banner>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose legal">
      <h2>Technical Source Online Privacy Statement</h2>
      <p>Technical Source respects your privacy and is committed to protect the personal information that you share with us. Generally, you can browse through our website without giving us any information about yourself. When we do need your personal information to provide services that you request or when you choose to provide us with your personal information, this policy describes how we collect and use your personal information. Our <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms of Use</a> cover the rest of how our website may be used.</p>

      <h2>Information Collection</h2>
      <p>Personal information means any information that may be used to identify an individual, including, but not limited to: first and last name, email address, home, postal or other physical address, other contact information, title, birth date, gender, occupation, industry, personal interests, and other information when needed to provide a service you requested.</p>
      <p>When you browse our website, you do so anonymously. We don’t automatically collect personal information, including your email address. We may log your IP address (the Internet address of your computer) to give us an idea of which part of our website you visit and how long you spend there, but we do not link your IP address to any personal information. Like many other commercial websites, the Technical Source website may from time to time use a standard technology called a “cookie” to collect information about how you use the site. Please go to “Cookies and Tracking Technology” below for more information.</p>
      <p>Technical Source collects personal information when you send us a form on our website (a contact request, a job application, a resume, a referral or a request to talk to a person from our chat assistant), when you use certain Technical Source online products or services, or when you submit your personal information to Technical Source for any other reason. SMS consent or phone numbers will not be shared with any third parties.</p>

      <h2>Forms on Our Website</h2>
      <p>When you send a form on our website, the information you enter (and any resume you attach) is sent to our team by email and saved in the systems we use to manage candidates, clients and inquiries: our recruiting system (Crelate) and our own system, TS Workspace. We use it to answer your request, consider you for current and future opportunities, and follow up with you. If someone refers you to us, we receive your name and contact details from them, along with what they tell us about you.</p>
      <p>With a form, we also receive a short note on how you found our website: the site or campaign link that brought you here, the first page you visited and when, how many pages you viewed and the industry you showed interest in. This is kept in your own browser until you send a form, and is not sent to us otherwise.</p>

      <h2>Our Chat Assistant</h2>
      <p>Our website offers a chat assistant that answers questions about Technical Source and our open positions. Its answers are generated by artificial intelligence (Claude, provided by Anthropic), so the messages you type are sent to that provider to produce a reply. Your conversation is kept in your browser tab and is not stored on our servers. If you choose to talk to a person, the details you enter and the conversation are sent to our team, as with our other forms. Please don’t share sensitive personal information in the chat.</p>

      <h2>Notice</h2>
      <p>When personal information is collected, we will inform you at the point of collection the purpose for the collection. Technical Source will not transfer your personal information to third parties without your consent, except under the limited conditions described under the discussion entitled “Information Sharing and Disclosure” below. SMS consent or phone numbers will not be shared with any third parties.</p>
      <p>Your information stays in the United States: we store and process it in the U.S., through the service providers described under “Information Sharing and Disclosure.”</p>
      <p>We will always give you the opportunity to “opt out” of receiving direct marketing or market research information. This means we assume you have given us your consent to collect and use your information in accordance with this Policy unless you take affirmative action to indicate that you do not consent, for instance by clicking or checking the appropriate option or box at the point of collection. In some cases, when applicable, we will provide you with the opportunity to “opt in.” This means we will require your affirmative action to indicate your consent before we use your information for purposes other than the purpose for which it was submitted.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and Tracking Technology</h2>
      <p>A cookie is a small data file that certain websites write to your hard drive when you visit them. A cookie file can contain information such as a user ID that the site uses to track the pages you’ve visited, but the only personal information a cookie can contain is information you supply yourself. A cookie can’t read data off your hard disk or read cookie files created by other sites. Some parts of Technical Source’s website use cookies to track user traffic patterns. We do this in order to determine the usefulness of our website information to our users and to see how effective our navigational structure is in helping users reach that information.</p>
      <p>We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use our website, and the LinkedIn Insight Tag to measure how well our LinkedIn posts and advertising reach the people they’re meant for. Both use cookies and report visits to us in summary form; they do not tell us who you are. You can opt out of Google Analytics with Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">browser add-on</a>, and manage LinkedIn advertising in your <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/psettings/guest-controls" rel="noopener">LinkedIn settings</a>.</p>
      <p>Our website also uses your browser’s own storage (local storage) to remember the industry you’re interested in, so we can show you the most relevant stories first, and how you found our website, as described under “Forms on Our Website.” This stays on your device; you can remove it at any time by clearing your browser’s data for our website.</p>
      <p>If you prefer not to receive cookies while browsing our website, you can set your browser to warn you before accepting cookies and refuse the cookie when your browser alerts you to its presence. You can also refuse all cookies by turning them off in your browser, although you may not be able to take full advantage of Technical Source’s website if you do so. In particular, you may be required to accept cookies in order to complete certain actions on our website. You do not need to have cookies turned on, however, to use or navigate through many parts of our website.</p>

      <h2>SMS Messaging Consent</h2>
      <p>By providing your mobile number, you agree to receive text messages from Technical Source, LLC at the number provided. Messages may include updates, alerts, promotions, and reminders. Standard message and data rates may apply. You can opt out at any time by replying STOP. For help, reply HELP.</p>
      <p>I agree to receive text messages from Technical Source, LLC, upon submission of my resume or contact information directly or through any third party vendors contracted to perform work on behalf of Technical Source. SMS consent or phone numbers will not be shared with any third parties. Please follow the link below to confirm you agree to text messaging from Technical Source, LLC.</p>
      <p><a href="https://forms.office.com/r/CaReYGmq9W" rel="noopener">Confirm Text Messaging Consent</a></p>

      <h2>Information Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
      <p>Technical Source does not disclose personally identifying information other than as described in this policy. Visitors can always refuse to supply personally identifying information, with the caveat that it may prevent them from engaging in certain website-related activities or services.</p>
      <p>We don’t sell your personal information. We share it only:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>with service providers who help us run our business: website hosting, email, our applicant and client systems, our chat assistant’s AI provider and website analytics. They receive only the information they need and are bound to use it only for us;</li>
        <li>when you ask us to, for example when we present you to a client for a role you’ve agreed to be considered for;</li>
        <li>when the law requires it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>Technical Source safeguards the security of the data you send us with physical, electronic, and managerial procedures. Every page of our website uses industry-standard encryption (HTTPS) to protect data in transit. While we strive to protect your personal information, no method of sending or storing information over the Internet is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee the security of the information you send us.</p>

      <h2>Children and Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our websites do not target and are not intended to attract children under the age of 13. Technical Source does not knowingly solicit personal information from children under the age of 13 or send them requests for personal information.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Sites</h2>
      <p>Technical Source’s website contains links to other sites. Technical Source does not share your personal information with those websites and is not responsible for their privacy practices. We encourage you to learn about the privacy policies of those companies.</p>
      <p>Once you have left our website, check the other website’s own privacy policy to see how it handles any information it collects from you.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>Technical Source will amend this policy from time to time. If we make any substantial changes in the way we use your personal information, we will make that information available by posting a notice on this site.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>For questions about this policy, or to ask us to update or delete your personal information, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
